Notebook[{
Cell["EmbeddingClosest", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"514dcfed-7148-4195-95a5-64107b08b7e3"],

Cell["[LLM Generated]", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"bea5b282-4d1e-4a33-8a13-efb7b5e5eb39"],

Cell["\<\
EmbeddingClosest[graph, bundle, {p1, p2}] keeps the bundle elements whose \
drawing under GraphEmbedding is Hausdorff-closest to the straight Euclidean \
segment p1-p2. EmbeddingClosest[graph, bundle, {center, radius}] keeps the \
bundle elements Hausdorff-closest to the Euclidean circle of given centre and \
radius. EmbeddingClosest[graph, bundle, curve] keeps the bundle elements \
Hausdorff-closest to an arbitrary embedded curve, where curve is a Line / \
BSplineCurve / BezierCurve or a list of at least three plane points in the \
embedding's coordinates. Dispatch is by reference shape: {vertex, vertex} for \
paths, {vertex, numeric} for cycles, a curve or >=3-point list for the \
best-approximating path. Accepts bare lists, InfraSegment / InfraLine / \
InfraPath / InfraRay / InfraCircle wrappers, or homogeneous lists of unary \
wrappers; wrappers are preserved. Operator form EmbeddingClosest[graph, \
ref][bundle].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"936d36c8-6431-4371-b0b8-a798e9b1c0c8"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f3c46a8c-c768-42cc-85cf-5e3c3bb39797"],

Cell["Load the paclet.", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"ef94c463-c73e-4bf3-8f17-976b5549a2a2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`SyntheticInfrageometry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Code",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"ecda1e97-4d6d-4a39-9c93-d99cbee35c8e"],

Cell["Related Guides", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7adb4d4e-46b6-4ed1-bd94-b48076be1330"],

Cell["PathSpaceGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"21c5f491-d258-4f08-8470-42ac8efdb21d"],

Cell["SyntheticInfrageometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3f70d449-37da-41f9-bfe3-5002e849f02e"]
},
